{"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Instance Method","externalID":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P14ColoringModuleE04edgeC0AD04EdgeC0VyxGyF","extendedModule":"GraphProtocols","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"edgeColoring"},{"kind":"text","text":"() -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"EdgeColoring","preciseIdentifier":"s:14ColoringModule04EdgeA0V"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":">"}],"remoteSource":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/ColoringModule\/EdgeColoring.swift#L479","fileName":"EdgeColoring.swift"},"title":"edgeColoring()","modules":[{"name":"ColoringModule","relatedModules":["GraphProtocols"]}],"symbolKind":"method","role":"symbol"},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/edgeColoring()","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An edge colouring with at most Δ + 1 colours (Vizing’s bound), by Misra and Gries’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"constructive proof. Edges in position order, each coloured through a fan at its end with the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"lesser vertex index, every choice the least colour or vertex available. At least Δ colours"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"always, and Δ + 1 on class-2 graphs (odd cycles, odd complete graphs, Petersen), but"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"sometimes Δ + 1 on class-1 graphs too (K(4)); on a bipartite graph "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"bipartiteEdgeColoring()"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"always gives Δ. O(m · (Δ² + n)) time: a fan has at most Δ vertices, each found among the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"edges at u, and a path at most n edges. O(n + m) memory. For a multigraph"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"digraph.undirectedView"},{"type":"text","text":" with an antiparallel pair is one), use "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"greedyEdgeColoring()"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"sections":[],"kind":"symbol","hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule","doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule\/GraphProtocols","doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule\/GraphProtocols\/Graph"]]},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"edgeColoring","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() -> ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:14ColoringModule04EdgeA0V","text":"EdgeColoring","identifier":"doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule\/EdgeColoring","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">","kind":"text"}],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"content":[{"level":2,"text":"Discussion","type":"heading","anchor":"discussion"},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The graph is simple: no self-loops, no parallel edges.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"name":"Precondition","style":"note","type":"aside"}],"kind":"content"}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/coloringmodule\/graphprotocols\/graph\/edgecoloring()"]}],"references":{"doc://ColoringModule/documentation/ColoringModule":{"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/coloringmodule","identifier":"doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule","title":"ColoringModule","type":"topic","abstract":[],"role":"collection"},"doc://ColoringModule/documentation/ColoringModule/GraphProtocols/Graph":{"url":"\/documentation\/coloringmodule\/graphprotocols\/graph","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"extension"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Graph","preciseIdentif